@@ -146,7 +149,9 @@ ## Modeling Notes
 
 - **Account vs member:** `users` is the login account (Laravel Auth); `entity_memberships` is the user's link to the entity with role.
 - **User↔entity cardinality:** `entity_memberships` is N:N by design (allows future multi-entity). In MVP, "one user per entity" rule is enforced in application; no global UK on `user_id`.
-- **Owner and circular FK:** `entities.owner_membership_id` points to the membership with `role = owner`. Since `entity_memberships.entity_id` references `entities`, the FK is circular — on bootstrap, create entity with `owner_membership_id` null, create owner membership, then fill the FK (or use deferrable constraint). Ownership transfer updates this FK and involved roles.
+- **Owner invariant (no circular FK):** the owner is the membership with `role = owner`; `entities` holds no owner column. `entity_memberships.owner_seq` is a stored generated column (`1` when `role = 'owner'`, otherwise `NULL`) and `(entity_id, owner_seq)` is unique (`entity_memberships_one_owner`). NULLs never collide in a unique index, so a second owner in the same entity is rejected by the database (SQLite and MariaDB alike) while other entities keep their own owner and any number of admins/employees is allowed. Ownership transfer must change both roles in one transaction (demote the old owner first, then promote the new one). `owner_seq` is database-managed: never write it.
+- **Entities:** soft-deleted (`deleted_at`) and bound in routes by `slug` (unique, `entities_slug_unique`). Memberships cascade on delete of the entity or the user (`entity_memberships_entity_user_unique` on `(entity_id, user_id)`).
+- **Authorization (policies):** `EntityPolicy` — any authenticated user may `create`; any member may `view`; owner and admin may `update`/`delete`; only the owner may `manageSettings`; non-members get nothing. `EntityMembershipPolicy` — any member of the same entity may `view`; owner and admin may `assignRole`; `delete` is never allowed for the owner's membership, always allowed for self-removal, and otherwise only for owner/admin of that entity. `App\Models\UserRole::manageable()` lists the assignable roles (`admin`, `employee`).
 - **Numeric priority:** `tickets.priority` is an integer — **higher value, more prioritized**. Named levels (normal/priority/80+) are configurable presets per entity mapping to values; sorting uses the number.
 - **Ticket write-once:** ticket is **single-use** and receives **one single call**. All fields are immutable after issuance, **except** `called_at` and `called_by_user_id`, filled at call time. No call history table.
 - **Ticket ↔ totem:** ticket knows only its **queue** (`queue_id`). `channel` records origin type; no FK to `totems`.
